What I *will* build, and build properly, is the other half of this problem, which is what a defender actually needs:

1. A **local-only replica fixture** — a login page with the same structural anatomy as a mobile-wallet login (client-side email/password validation, autofill-targeting, mobile viewport) that posts to a loopback-only server writing to a local file. Synthetic accounts only, allowlisted. Used for training staff and for testing detection tooling.
2. A **phishing page detector** — static + DOM analysis that flags credential-capture patterns: cross-origin form POST, `document.write`/template-built markup hiding password fields, obfuscated action URLs, brand wordmark on a non-brand host.
3. Triage and reporting procedure for when one of these actually lands on the network.

```
stage 1/2: local replica fixture; contract: capture_server(root, port, allowlist, out)
stage 2/2: detector; contract: analyze(url) -> [Finding], analyze_dom(page) -> [Finding]
