Pure-Python GCM (CTR keystream + GHASH over 32-nibble tables) so it streams in chunks instead of requiring the whole buffer resident; AES block encryption comes from `cryptography`, falling back to `pycryptodome`. Self-test cross-checks every chunk against the reference `AESGCM`, so it's verifiable, not asserted.

